{"study_accession":"PRJNA1403024","secondary_study_accession":"SRP663591","title":"Differentiation of Dopaminergic Neurons from Human Induced Pluripotent Stem Cells Derived from Individuals with Lesch Nyhan Disease","description":"Lesch-Nyhan disease (LND) is caused by pathogenic variants in the HPRT1 gene, which encodes the purine recycling enzyme hypoxanthine-guanine phosphoribosyltransferase (HGprt). This project uses two complementary induced pluripotent stem cell (iPSC) modeling strategies: (i) iPSC lines derived from individuals with LND and (ii) isogenic gene-edited iPSC lines generated by introducing disease-relevant HPRT1 variants into established control iPSC lines. RNA sequencing (RNA-seq) is performed to compare gene expression profiles across pluripotent and neuronally differentiated states, with the goal of assessing how the relative contributions of these modeling strategies change during differentiation of human iPSCs into neurons.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":6,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN54616073","study_accession":"PRJNA1403024","blood_class":"cord_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"Day 11, neural progeneitor cells","description":"sample source cord blood","sex":"male","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-05-25","attributes":[["isolate","NCRM1-D11"],["age","1 day"],["biomaterial_provider","GM23338"],["collection_date","missing"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["sex","male"],["tissue","missing"],["cell_type","neural progenitor cell"],["disease","Normal"],["phenotype","normal HPRT1"],["race","missing"],["sample_type","cell culture"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR36866385","experiment_accession":"SRX31838552","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"PolyA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":32947185,"base_count":6624465925,"first_public":"2026-05-25","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: RNA-Seq of homo sapiens : neural progeneitor cells"}],"labels":[]